## Your target

For most adults under 80, the aim is a reading **below 140/90** at the surgery, or **below 135/85** at home. For people aged 80 or over, the target is usually **below 150/90** (145/85 at home). Your doctor may set a different target for you.

## Healthy changes

These help everyone with high blood pressure, and can be enough on their own for some people:

- **cut down on salt** to less than 6g (about a teaspoon) a day, including salt already in food
- **eat plenty of fruit and vegetables**
- **be active**, aiming for 150 minutes of moderate activity a week
- **lose weight** if you need to
- **drink less alcohol**, no more than 14 units a week
- **stop smoking**
- **cut down on caffeine**

## Medicines

Many people need medicine as well. The main types are:

| Type | Examples | How it works |
| --- | --- | --- |
| ACE inhibitors | ramipril, lisinopril | relax blood vessels |
| Angiotensin receptor blockers (ARBs) | losartan, candesartan | relax blood vessels |
| Calcium channel blockers | amlodipine | widen blood vessels |
| Diuretics | indapamide | remove extra water and salt |

Which one you start on depends on things like your **age**, **ethnicity**, and whether you have **diabetes**. Many people need two or three medicines to reach their target. It can take a few tries to find the right mix.

{% callout type="warn" title="Taking your medicine" %}
Blood pressure medicine only works while you keep taking it, even though you may feel no different. If you get side effects, talk to your GP or pharmacist rather than stopping.
{% /callout %}

## Checking at home

Your GP may ask you to check your blood pressure at home. Use a **validated upper arm monitor**. Sit quietly for 5 minutes first, and take two readings a minute apart. Write down your readings to show your GP or nurse.

## Regular reviews

You should have your blood pressure and medicines reviewed at least **once a year**, usually with blood tests to check your kidneys.

Next, read about [living well with high blood pressure](/conditions/physical/high-blood-pressure/living-well/).
